# CFF 1.2.0: entity form not yet supported; use person with family-names.
# This represents the Knovaryn maintainers as a collective.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Knovaryn, please cite it as below."
# No DOI yet: one will be added only after a real DOI is registered for a
# public archive snapshot. Fabricated placeholder DOIs are not acceptable.
title: "Knovaryn"
abstract: >-
  Open, MCP-native training-data foundry: turn permitted documents into
  traceable, quality-gated SFT and preference datasets via CLI, MCP server,
  REST API, and web console. Every training example, traced to its source.
authors:
  # Organization represented as person with family-names (entity form
  # requires CFF 1.3.0, not yet supported by cffconvert)
  - family-names: "Knovaryn maintainers"
keywords:
  - MCP
  - training-data
  - SFT
  - preference-data
  - DPO
  - dataset
  - LLM
  - provenance
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: 2026-08-25
version: 0.2.1
repository-code: "https://github.com/waalwalker1/knovaryn"
url: "https://waalwalker1.github.io/knovaryn/"
